<myopenmath xmlns:pi="http://pretextbook.org/2020/pretext/internal" id="1468692">
<statement>
<p>Solve this system of equations using substitution.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle-{7}{x}+{4}{y}=-{54}</m> </p>
<p>
  <m>\displaystyle-{2}{x}-{6}{y}={6}</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="8"/></p>

</statement>
<answer>
<p><ul><li><m>\displaystyle{\left({6},-{3}\right)}</m></li></ul></p>
</answer>
<solution><p>We chose (for no special reason) to solve the first equation for <m>\displaystyle{x}</m>.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle-{7}{x}+{4}{y}=-{54}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle-{7}{x}=-{54}-{\left({4}{y}\right)}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{x}=\frac{{-{54}-{\left({4}{y}\right)}}}{{-{{7}}}}</m></p>
<p>Then we can substitute this into the second equation.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle-{2}{\left(\frac{{-{54}-{\left({4}{y}\right)}}}{{-{{7}}}}\right)}+-{6}{y}={6}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle-\frac{{2}}{{-{{7}}}}\cdot{\left(-{54}\right)}--\frac{{2}}{{-{{7}}}}{\left({4}\right)}{y}+-{6}{y}={6}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle-{15.428571428571}-{\left(-{1.1428571428571}\right)}{y}+-{6}{y}={6}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle-{1.1428571428571}{y}+{\left(-{6}\right)}{y}={6}--{15.428571428571}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle-{1.1428571428571}{y}+{\left(-{6}\right)}{y}={21.428571428571}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{\left(-{1.1428571428571}+{\left(-{6}\right)}\right)}{y}={21.428571428571}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle-{7.1428571428571}{y}={21.428571428571}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{y}=\frac{{21.428571428571}}{{-{{7.1428571428571}}}}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{y}=-{3}</m></p>
<p>Finally we can substitute this y value into the first equation to solve for x.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle-{7}{x}+{4}{\left(-{3}\right)}=-{54}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle-{7}{x}+{\left(-{12}\right)}=-{54}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle-{7}{x}=-{54}-{\left(-{12}\right)}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle-{7}{x}=-{42}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{x}=-\frac{{42}}{{-{{7}}}}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{x}={6}</m></p>
<p>Thus the answer is <m>\displaystyle{\left({6},-{3}\right)}</m>.</p>
</solution>
</myopenmath>